@startuml 09-seq-ask-reminder-escalation
!include style.iuml
title A question with a deadline: reminder and escalation by the clock

actor "Engineer (Ana)" as Eng
participant "coordination_ask" as TAsk
database "Ledger" as Ledger
participant "Deliverer" as Deliver
actor "Coordinator" as Coord
participant "Clock" as Clock
actor "Product manager" as PM
participant "coordination_answer" as TAnswer

Eng -> TAsk : to coordinator, text, item W…
TAsk -> Ledger : append message.sent {kind ask,\nneedsAnswerBy = now + 1 block}
TAsk -> Deliver : enqueue
Deliver -> Coord : steer: QUESTION from Ana (record 8f3a…)
TAsk --> Eng : "Asked; record 8f3a…; the plugin follows up"

== 1 block later, no answer ==
Clock -> Ledger : messages with needsAnswerBy < now and answeredBy = null
Clock -> Ledger : append clock.reminder {message 8f3a…}
Clock -> Deliver : enqueue(same text, "(resent)", to coordinator)
Deliver -> Coord : steer: QUESTION (resent) 8f3a…
Clock -> Deliver : enqueue(note to Ana: "no answer yet; reminded")

== 2 blocks later, still no answer ==
Clock -> Ledger : append clock.escalated {message 8f3a…, to product-manager}
Clock -> Deliver : enqueue(copy to product manager)
Deliver -> PM : steer: ESCALATED question 8f3a… from Ana to coordinator
note right of PM
  A PM→coordinator message escalates into
  the owner bundle instead (see 17).
end note

== the answer ==
Coord -> TAnswer : message 8f3a…, text
TAnswer -> Ledger : append message.answered
TAnswer -> Deliver : enqueue(answer → Ana, item W…)
Deliver -> Eng : steer: ANSWER to 8f3a… (record 9c1d…)
TAnswer --> Coord : "Answered"
note over Ledger
  Nobody counted blocks, resent by hand,
  or copied anyone: four events did it.
end note
@enduml
